  "description": "BIZCUK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H108 Gd4 N23 Ni4 O36 2+,2(N3 1-),10(H2 O1),C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Ni1 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.523-4.942 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.97-173.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H129N33O45Ni4Gd4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 0 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
